IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hpr-law`
IMPORT `hpr-seat`
IMPORT `hpr-seat-practitioner`

-- Health Practitioner Regulation (Adoption of National Law) Act 2009 (NSW) -- worked cases for every exported question
-- of the practitioner's seat (hpr-seat-practitioner.l4), with mirror cases: the same facts asked from the complainant's
-- seat (hpr-seat.l4) and the practitioner's, with answers that agree.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `practitioner cases`

`day` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY

`critical suspension` MEANS `the Council must suspend my registration until the Tribunal deals with it, and refer it to the Tribunal as a complaint`
`council meeting` MEANS `the Council at an inquiry at a Council meeting`
`PSC` MEANS `a Professional Standards Committee`
`AC` MEANS `an Assessment Committee`
`rejected request` MEANS `a rejection of my request because it was made in a period when requests were not permitted`

`named entity` MEANS `a Committee, a Performance Review Panel, the Tribunal or its List Manager, the Supreme Court, or another body s 163A(4) names`
`a Council, Subdivision 5, Division 8 or s 155C(1)(f)` MEANS `a Council, at an inquiry at a Council meeting, on a review, or with my consent after a performance assessment`
`a Council, s 150` MEANS `a Council, under another provision, such as urgent action under section 150`

§§ `s 150 -- urgent action`

-- Arguments: satisfied for protection or the public interest, satisfied of a critical compliance breach.
#ASSERT `Must the Council act against me now` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `critical suspension`
#ASSERT `Must the Council act against me now` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `critical suspension`
#ASSERT `Must the Council act against me now` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Council must suspend my registration or impose conditions on it`
#ASSERT `Must the Council act against me now` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `section 150 does not authorise action against me on these facts`

§§ `s 150A -- review by the Council`

#ASSERT `What must the Council do on my review application` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the Council may refuse to reconsider: it thinks my application frivolous or vexatious`
#ASSERT `What must the Council do on my review application` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the Council must reconsider, and may affirm, vary or set aside its decision`
#ASSERT `What must the Council do on my review application` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Council must reconsider, but can only affirm it: no change in my circumstances`

§§ `ss 159, 159B -- appeals against the Council`

#ASSERT `Can I appeal against the Council's decision` `a reprimand under Division 3` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against the Council's decision` `a suspension under Division 3, or a refusal to end one` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against the Council's decision` `conditions imposed under s 127AA or Division 3 or 4, or their alteration` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against the Council's decision` `a refusal of my s 150I request to alter or remove conditions` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against the Council's decision` `a direction or order at an inquiry at a Council meeting (s 148E)` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against the Council's decision` `a refusal of my s 152K request about impairment conditions or suspension` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 159(2): no appeal against a rejection of a request made in a barred period; s 159B still allows a point of law
-- appeal about action under s 150, 150A or 150C.
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against the Council's decision` `rejected request` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against the Council's decision` `rejected request` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against the Council's decision` `another decision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against the Council's decision` `another decision` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `ss 158, 158A, 161, 161B -- appeals`

#ASSERT `Can I appeal against the Committee, as the practitioner` `PSC` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against the Committee, as the practitioner` `AC` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against the Committee, as the practitioner` `the Tribunal` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is my appeal in time, as the practitioner` (`day` 1 3 2026) (`day` 29 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS `in time: within 28 days`
#ASSERT `Is my appeal in time, as the practitioner` (`day` 1 3 2026) (`day` 30 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS `out of time, unless the Tribunal allows a longer period`
#ASSERT `Is my appeal in time, as the practitioner` (`day` 15 2 2026) (`day` 15 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS `in time: within 28 days`
#ASSERT `Is my appeal in time, as the practitioner` (`day` 15 2 2028) (`day` 15 3 2028) FALSE EQUALS `out of time, unless the Tribunal allows a longer period`
#ASSERT `Is my appeal in time, as the practitioner` (`day` 15 2 2028) (`day` 15 3 2028) TRUE EQUALS `in time only because the Tribunal allowed a longer period`
#ASSERT `Can I appeal on a point of law now, as the practitioner` `during the inquiry` (`day` 1 3 2026) (`day` 29 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I appeal on a point of law now, as the practitioner` `during the inquiry` (`day` 1 3 2026) (`day` 30 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I appeal on a point of law now, as the practitioner` `after the inquiry was completed` (`day` 1 3 2026) (`day` 2 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does the decision still bind me while I appeal` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the decision still bind me while I appeal` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 163A -- review of orders`

-- Arguments: order, who made it, order says no review yet, appeal pending.
#ASSERT `Can I apply for review of the order` `a prohibition order` `a Council, s 150` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I apply for review of the order` `a suspension of my registration` `named entity` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I apply for review of the order` `conditions on my registration` `a Council, Subdivision 5, Division 8 or s 155C(1)(f)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 163A(4)(b1): a Council counts "but only" for orders under Division 8, Subdivision 5 of Division 3 or s 155C(1)(f);
-- an urgent suspension or conditions under s 150 is not a relevant order.
#ASSERT `Can I apply for review of the order` `a suspension of my registration` `a Council, s 150` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I apply for review of the order` `conditions on my registration` `a Council, s 150` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I apply for review of the order` `a cancellation of my registration, or a disqualification from registration` `named entity` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I apply for review of the order` `a suspension of my registration` `another body, such as a National Board` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I apply for review of the order` `a cancellation of my registration, or a disqualification from registration` `named entity` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I apply for review of the order` `conditions on my registration` `named entity` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I apply for review of the order` `an order made on an earlier review` `another body, such as a National Board` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I apply for review of the order` `another order` `named entity` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I apply for review of the order` `another order` `named entity` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 149C(4A), 149E -- registering again`

-- Arguments: cancelled or disqualified by the Tribunal, reinstatement order, within a would-have-been suspension.
-- s 149E(2): a disqualification that has run its course still needs a reinstatement order.
#ASSERT `Can I apply to be registered again` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I apply to be registered again` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I apply to be registered again` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I apply to be registered again` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I apply to be registered again` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 145F, 147C(3) -- not complying with a direction`

#ASSERT `What follows if I did not comply` `a direction to attend counselling (s 145B(1)(g))` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `it is evidence that I lack sufficient physical or mental capacity to practise`
#ASSERT `What follows if I did not comply` `a direction to undergo an examination (s 145E)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `it is evidence that I lack sufficient physical or mental capacity to practise`
#ASSERT `What follows if I did not comply` `a notice to undergo skills testing (s 147C)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `it is evidence that I lack sufficient skill to practise`
#ASSERT `What follows if I did not comply` `a notice to undergo skills testing (s 147C)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the Act draws no such inference`
#ASSERT `What follows if I did not comply` `a direction to undergo an examination (s 145E)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Act draws no such inference`

§§ `Fines, representation, notice, costs`

#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined` `medical` `the Tribunal` `professional misconduct` TRUE FALSE 110 EQUALS JUST 27500
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined` `another registered health profession` `council meeting` `unsatisfactory professional conduct` TRUE FALSE 110 EQUALS JUST 5500
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined` `medical` `PSC` `unsatisfactory professional conduct` TRUE TRUE 110 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `Can I have a lawyer, as the practitioner` `council meeting` EQUALS `not entitled to be legally represented, but may be accompanied by a support person, who can be an Australian lawyer`
#ASSERT `Can I have a lawyer, as the practitioner` `the Tribunal` EQUALS `entitled to attend and to be represented by an Australian legal practitioner, or by another adviser with leave`
#ASSERT `Can I have a lawyer, as the practitioner` `AC` EQUALS `not entitled to be legally represented`
#ASSERT `Was I given enough notice, as the practitioner` (`day` 1 3 2026) (`day` 16 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Was I given enough notice, as the practitioner` (`day` 1 3 2026) (`day` 15 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to pay costs, as the practitioner` `the Tribunal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to pay costs, as the practitioner` `PSC` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Mirror cases -- the same facts from both seats`

-- The fine: a pharmacist, a Council meeting, unsatisfactory professional conduct, no other order appropriate.
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined` `pharmacy` `council meeting` `unsatisfactory professional conduct` TRUE FALSE 110 EQUALS `What is the most the practitioner can be fined` `pharmacy` `council meeting` `unsatisfactory professional conduct` TRUE FALSE 110
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined` `medical` `the Tribunal` `nothing proved or admitted` TRUE FALSE 110 EQUALS `What is the most the practitioner can be fined` `medical` `the Tribunal` `nothing proved or admitted` TRUE FALSE 110
-- Appeal timing: both sides appealing a Committee decision with reasons given the same day.
#ASSERT `Is my appeal in time, as the practitioner` (`day` 1 3 2026) (`day` 29 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS `Is my appeal in time` (`day` 1 3 2026) (`day` 29 3 2026) FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my appeal in time, as the practitioner` (`day` 1 3 2026) (`day` 30 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS `Is my appeal in time` (`day` 1 3 2026) (`day` 30 3 2026) FALSE
-- Appeal right against a Committee.
#ASSERT `Can I appeal against the Committee, as the practitioner` `PSC` EQUALS `Can I appeal against the Committee's decision` `PSC`
-- Representation before the Tribunal and a Professional Standards Committee is the same for both; at a Council meeting it differs (finding 5).
#ASSERT `Can I have a lawyer, as the practitioner` `PSC` EQUALS `Can I have a lawyer at the hearing` `PSC`
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I have a lawyer, as the practitioner` `council meeting` EQUALS `Can I have a lawyer at the hearing` `council meeting`)
-- Notice of a Professional Standards Committee inquiry, given to both on the same day.
#ASSERT `Was I given enough notice, as the practitioner` (`day` 20 2 2026) (`day` 7 3 2026) EQUALS `Was I given enough notice of the inquiry` (`day` 20 2 2026) (`day` 7 3 2026)
-- Costs before the Tribunal.
#ASSERT `Can I be ordered to pay costs, as the practitioner` `the Tribunal` EQUALS `Can I be ordered to pay costs` `the Tribunal`
